From 56c02a462635146b3f99d5b44c3f971f6f8843c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: teeworlds-rl <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:42:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add an RL environment bridge driven over a unix socket

Phase 1 of the teeworlds-rl project. When sv_rl_socket is set the
server connects to a trainer, adds two server side players and runs
them in lockstep: every sv_rl_action_ticks ticks it sends observations
and event counts and waits for the next pair of actions. Without
sv_rl_socket nothing changes.

- CRlEnv (game/server/rlenv.*) owns the socket, the fixed size binary
  protocol, the agents and episode resets. Resets go through the same
  path as the restart command, so world, scores and respawn timers are
  reset by the game itself.
- Actions go through CPlayer::OnDirectInput and OnPredictedInput like
  network input; fire is counted per press and release like the client.
- CCharacter::TakeDamage and Die report damage, kills and suicides to
  the bridge. They only observe, game logic is unchanged.
- Protocol errors, a lost trainer and sv_rl_timeout shut the server
  down. sv_rl_debug enables a test only kill command.
